actor Caller
participant "Entry thread" as Entry
participant "Async object\nFuture / callback / message" as Async
participant "Executor / Scheduler" as Exec
participant "Work owner\nActor / Queue / DAO" as Owner
participant "Completion callback" as Callback

Caller -> Entry: request / message
Entry -> Async: create pending state
Entry -> Exec: submit / tell / send
Entry --> Caller: return without end-to-end completion
Exec -> Owner: execute work
Owner --> Async: set / setException / response message
Async -> Exec: schedule callback
Exec -> Callback: onSuccess / onFailure
Callback -> Owner: next relation / Actor message / commit decision

note over Entry,Callback
The callback thread is selected by the explicit Executor.
directExecutor means the thread that completes or observes the Future.
Method return, callback success, broker acknowledgement and DB commit
are separate boundaries.
end note

