title MQTT Telemetry - Producer ACK Before Database Completion

actor Device
participant "Netty EventLoop" as Netty
participant MqttTransportHandler as Mqtt
participant DefaultTransportService as Transport
queue "Rule Engine producer" as Producer
queue Kafka
participant "transportCallbackExecutor" as TransportCb
participant "tb-rule-engine-consumer" as Consumer
participant "App/Tenant/Rule Actors" as Actors
participant TbMsgTimeseriesNode as TsNode
participant BaseTimeseriesService as TsService
participant "SQL/Cassandra workers" as Database
participant "ts-service-ts-callback" as TsCallback

Device -> Netty: MQTT PUBLISH telemetry
Netty -> Mqtt: processDevicePublish(...)
Mqtt -> Transport: process(session, PostTelemetryMsg, callback)
loop each timestamp group
  Transport -> Producer: send(ToRuleEngineMsg, MsgPackCallback)
  Producer -> Kafka: provider send
  Kafka --> Producer: producer acknowledgement
  Producer --> Transport: TbQueueCallback.onSuccess
end
Transport -> TransportCb: submit MQTT callback
TransportCb -> Mqtt: onSuccess
Mqtt -> Netty: write PUBACK when msgId > 0
Netty --> Device: PUBACK (QoS 1 only)

Consumer -> Kafka: poll records later
Kafka --> Consumer: message pack
Consumer -> Actors: tell QueueToRuleEngineMsg
Actors -> TsNode: onMsg(ctx, msg)
TsNode -> TsService: saveAndNotify(..., TelemetryNodeCallback)
TsNode --> Actors: return; message remains pending
TsService -> Database: partition + history + latest Futures
Database --> TsService: aggregate Future success/failure
TsService -> TsCallback: run main callback
TsCallback -> Actors: tellSuccess / tellFailure
Actors --> Consumer: terminal TbMsgCallback
Consumer -> Consumer: analyze processing strategy
Consumer -> Kafka: commitSync when decision is commit

note over Device,Database
QoS 1 PUBACK only confirms successful production to the Rule Engine queue.
It does not wait for Rule Engine consumption or telemetry persistence.
QoS 0 has no PUBACK completion point.
end note

@enduml

