title Rule Engine Node - Return, Relation and Terminal ACK

participant "rule-dispatcher" as RuleThread
participant RuleNodeActor as NodeActor
participant TbMsgTimeseriesNode as Node
participant DefaultTelemetrySubscriptionService as Telemetry
participant BaseTimeseriesService as Service
participant "DB Future" as DbFuture
participant "ts-service-ts-callback" as CallbackThread
participant "Rule Chain routing" as Routing
participant TbMsgPackProcessingContext as Pack

RuleThread -> NodeActor: process RuleChainToRuleNodeMsg
NodeActor -> Node: onMsg(ctx, msg)
Node -> Telemetry: saveAndNotify(..., callback)
Telemetry -> Service: save(...)
Service -> DbFuture: allAsList(partition, history, latest)
Node --> NodeActor: return immediately

alt all database Futures succeed
  DbFuture -> CallbackThread: execute FutureCallback
  CallbackThread -> Routing: ctx.tellSuccess(msg)
else any database Future fails
  DbFuture -> CallbackThread: execute FutureCallback
  CallbackThread -> Routing: ctx.tellFailure(msg, t)
end

loop downstream relations
  Routing -> NodeActor: next Rule Node message
end
Routing -> Pack: terminal TbMsgCallback success/failure

note over Node,Pack
Node.onMsg returning is not an ACK.
TelemetryNodeCallback completes one node operation.
Only terminal routing completes the original queue message callback.
end note

@enduml

