title REST Server-side RPC - DeferredResult, Actor Pending and Timeout

actor User
participant "Servlet request thread" as Http
participant AbstractRpcController as Controller
participant "access-validator" as Validator
participant TbCoreDeviceRpcService as CoreRpc
queue "Rule Engine/Core queues" as Queues
participant "Rule Engine RPC service" as ReRpc
participant "device-dispatcher" as DeviceDispatcher
participant DeviceActorMessageProcessor as DeviceActor
participant "Actor scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "Transport callback / EventLoop" as Transport
actor Device

User -> Http: POST server-side RPC
Http -> Controller: handleDeviceRPCRequest(...)
Controller -> Controller: create DeferredResult
Controller -> Validator: validate(..., callback)
Controller --> Http: return DeferredResult
Http --> User: connection remains async

Validator -> CoreRpc: processRestApiRpcRequest
CoreRpc -> CoreRpc: store local response callback
CoreRpc -> Queues: RPC_CALL_FROM_SERVER_TO_DEVICE
Queues -> ReRpc: Rule Engine processing
ReRpc -> Queues: route to target Core
Queues -> DeviceDispatcher: high-priority Actor message
DeviceDispatcher -> DeviceActor: processRpcRequest
DeviceActor -> DeviceActor: pendingMap.put(requestId, metadata)
DeviceActor -> Scheduler: schedule timeout message
DeviceActor -> Transport: ToTransportMsg
Transport -> Device: protocol RPC request

alt device responds before expiration
  Device --> Transport: response payload
  Transport -> Queues: response to Core
  Queues -> DeviceDispatcher: response Actor message
  DeviceDispatcher -> DeviceActor: remove pending request
  DeviceActor -> CoreRpc: FromDeviceRpcResponse
  CoreRpc -> ReRpc: route response callback
  ReRpc -> Controller: reply callback
  Controller -> Http: DeferredResult.setResult
else timeout message wins
  Scheduler -> DeviceDispatcher: tell(timeoutMsg)
  DeviceDispatcher -> DeviceActor: remove pending request
  DeviceActor -> CoreRpc: TIMEOUT / NO_ACTIVE_CONNECTION
  CoreRpc -> Controller: reply callback
  Controller -> Http: DeferredResult.setResult(error)
end
Http --> User: async dispatch writes HTTP response

note over DeviceActor,Scheduler
The scheduler submits a timeout message. State removal normally belongs
to DeviceActor processing. Edge RPC contains blocking Future.get() calls
inside the DeviceActor path and can occupy the shared dispatcher.
end note

@enduml

