title PostgreSQL / TimescaleDB - JVM Queue, Transaction and Future

participant "DAO caller" as Dao
participant TbSqlBlockingQueueWrapper as Wrapper
queue TbSqlBlockingQueue as SqlQueue
participant "sql-queue-* single worker" as Worker
participant "Transactional insert repository" as Repository
database "PostgreSQL / TimescaleDB" as Pg
participant "ts-service-ts-callback" as TsCallback

Dao -> Wrapper: add(entity)
Wrapper -> SqlQueue: select queue by entity hash
SqlQueue -> SqlQueue: create SettableFuture + enqueue
SqlQueue --> Dao: pending Future

Worker -> SqlQueue: poll(maxDelay) first element
Worker -> SqlQueue: drainTo(batchSize - 1)
Worker -> Repository: saveFunction.accept(batch)
Repository -> Pg: JDBC batch in Spring transaction
alt transaction commits
  Pg --> Repository: commit
  Repository --> Worker: return
  Worker -> SqlQueue: future.set(null) for every element
  SqlQueue -> TsCallback: aggregate Future callback
else save or commit throws
  Pg --> Repository: rollback/error
  Repository --> Worker: Throwable
  Worker -> SqlQueue: future.setException(t) for every element
end

opt batch was not full
  Worker -> Worker: sleep remaining maxDelay after write
end

note over Dao,Pg
add() means JVM enqueue only. A successful queue Future is set after
the transactional repository method returns. Futures.allAsList across
partition/history/latest does not create a cross-DAO transaction.
end note

@enduml

