title Kafka Consumer - Poll, Actor Callback, Decision and Commit

queue Kafka
participant "tb-rule-engine-consumer" as Consumer
participant TbMsgPackProcessingContext as Pack
participant "Actor dispatchers" as Actors
participant "Rule Node callback executor" as NodeCallback
participant "Processing Strategy" as Strategy

Consumer -> Kafka: poll
Kafka --> Consumer: records
Consumer -> Pack: create pendingMap and latch
loop each record
  Consumer -> Actors: tell QueueToRuleEngineMsg
end
Consumer -> Pack: await(packProcessingTimeout)

Actors -> NodeCallback: start async side effect
NodeCallback --> Pack: onSuccess / onFailure
Pack -> Pack: pending -> success/failed; countDown
Pack --> Consumer: all done or timeout
Consumer -> Strategy: analyze(success, failed, pending)

alt retry decision
  Strategy --> Consumer: reprocessMap
  Consumer -> Consumer: update submit strategy and optional sleep
  Consumer -> Actors: resubmit current JVM pack subset
else commit decision
  Strategy --> Consumer: commit
  Consumer -> Pack: cleanup
  Consumer -> Kafka: commitSync
end

note over Consumer,Kafka
Actor callback does not commit an offset. Retry is in-memory resubmission,
not a new Kafka poll or retry topic. Long retry cycles can exceed
max.poll.interval.ms. A crash between side effect and commit can replay.
end note

@enduml
